  "intro": "<p>These are real given names whose meaning is the moon, moonlight, the full moon or the crescent moon, from Latin, Greek, Turkish, Arabic, Persian, Sanskrit, Japanese, Hawaiian and more. Every meaning has been checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary, and the England and Wales rank shown beside a name comes from the ONS baby name figures.</p><p>Plenty of names are sold as moon names when they aren't. Diana and Phoebe belonged to moon goddesses but their names mean something else, and Celine has nothing to do with the moon at all. We've kept a few of these in, marked as uncertain, so you can see why.</p>",
